==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|convenient|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|conveniens||fit, suitable, convenient|lang=la}}, present participle of {{term|convenire||to come together, suit}}; see [[convene]] and compare [[covenant]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-convenient.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or pertaining to [[convenience]]; [[simple]]; [[easy]]; [[expedient]].
#: ''Fast food might be '''convenient''', but it's also very unhealthy.''

====Antonyms====
* [[inconvenient]]

====Related terms====
* [[convene]]
* [[convenience]]

